% M8-bits-encoding-T3 continuation (D-0134 section 8): reif_eq_branch_unsat.fzn over BITS.
% b <-> (x = y) and b <-> (x <> y) at once is unsatisfiable, and nothing about it is
% visible at level 0, so the search branches on b and every conflict below sits under that
% decision: the reifier's literal is load-bearing in every derived line (D-0057's finding,
% which this model carries to the bits arm). x and y are over 0..2 (width 2), so on bits
% at `--bits-above 0`: under b = 1 the int_ne_reif's disequality piece and the
% int_eq_reif's rows clash; under b = 0 the int_eq_reif's disequality piece and the
% int_ne_reif's rows do, each piece a two-half `pol` with the reifier as one more term.
var bool: b :: output_var;
var 0..2: x :: output_var;
var 0..2: y :: output_var;
constraint int_eq_reif(x, y, b);
constraint int_ne_reif(x, y, b);
solve satisfy;
